CLAUDE_REPLY_SKILL = r'''---
name: warp-reply
description: Reply to an incoming CCB request via Warp LocalAgentBus. Preferred over terminal markers.
metadata:
  short-description: Reply to a CCB request reliably
---

# Warp Reply - Submit Response

Use this when you receive a request containing `[CCB_REQ_ID:<id>]` to submit your response back to the Bus.

## Step 1: Prepare Reply

Complete the requested task. If the reply is long, save it to a temporary file.

## Step 2: Submit via warp-reply (PREFERRED)

```powershell
# File mode — recommended for long replies
warp-reply --req-id $REQ_ID --content-file $FILE_PATH

# Stdin mode — for short replies
echo "$CONTENT" | warp-reply --req-id $REQ_ID --stdin
```

Parameters:
- --req-id (required): The request ID from [CCB_REQ_ID:<id>]
- --content-file (optional): Path to file containing the reply
- --stdin (optional): Read reply content from standard input
- --content (optional): Inline text for very short replies only

## Step 3: Fallback to Markers (if warp-reply fails)

If warp-reply is not available or returns non-zero, fall back to terminal markers:

```
[CCB_START:reply-<REQ_ID>]
<your reply>
[CCB_END:reply-<REQ_ID>]
```

## Rules

- ALWAYS try warp-reply first. Only fall back to markers if the command fails.
- Do NOT use both warp-reply and markers for the same request.
- Prefer --content-file over --content to avoid shell escaping issues.
'''

CODEX_REPLY_SKILL = r'''---
name: warp-reply
description: Reply to an incoming CCB request via Warp LocalAgentBus. Preferred over terminal markers.
metadata:
  short-description: Reply to a CCB request reliably
---

# Warp Reply - Submit Response

Use this when you receive a request containing `[CCB_REQ_ID:<id>]` to submit your response back to the Bus.

